# The corpus's own regex-based parser splits on '\n' and anchors headings and
# table rows with '$', which does not cross a '\r'. A Windows checkout without
# this file silently converts every text file to CRLF and breaks that parsing
# with no error at the point of conversion — only later, deep in a track or
# table lookup. Force LF everywhere so the parser sees what git stored.
* text=auto eol=lf
